kly digest of Ukrainian commentary and analysis from across the political spectrum, only for War on the Rocks&#160;members. Each Monday, we bring you a curated selection of articles fr', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/why-the-weeks-most-important-story-went-unwritten/'}, {'signal_id': '5f06bd2df0b6d0ab', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Collective Defense in an Era of Tokens and Data Links <p>NATO&#8217;s Supreme Allied Commander Transformation, Adm. Pierre Vandier, returns to the studio to discuss how the alliance is continuously adapting to a new era of warfare driven by software, data, and uncrewed systems, a', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/collective-defense-in-an-era-of-tokens-and-data-links/'}, {'signal_id': 'd1016e746dc68955', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Speed to Fielding Is Not Speed to Combat Power <p>I spent more than 20 years in U.S. Army air defense, much of it in cramped control stations where the difference between a successful engagement and a catastrophic loss came down to the soldier at the console. The radar did its jo', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/speed-to-fielding-is-not-speed-to-combat-power/'}, {'signal_id': 'ec28565eed6fe31f', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Tracing the Future Soldier’s Tech Stack <p>Movies, shows, and books have long been at the forefront of imagining the future of war. If you were to picture the &#8220;future soldier,&#8221; you&#8217;d likely picture the genetically engineered super soldiers that have captivated &', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/tracing-the-future-soldiers-tech-stack/'}, {'signal_id': '9a636280e2613da0', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'What the Nvidia Scandal Reveals About Modern Espionage <p>Espionage is often called the world’s second-oldest profession. Its overlap with the first has now reached the frontier of artificial intelligence. Nvidia’s billionaire co-founder Jensen Huang, instantly recognisable by hi', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/what-the-nvidia-scandal-reveals-about-modern-espionage'}, {'signal_id': '33997ef9a65de045', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The Nvidia Spy Allegations Loom Over Trump's Meeting With Xi <p>Nvidia’s former CEO, Jensen Huang, and his extramarital relationship with the alleged Chinese agent Alice Huang, likely will be discussed at the scheduled meeting of President Donald Trump and Chinese President Xi Ji", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-nvidia-spy-allegations-loom-over-trump-s-meeting-with-xi'}, {'signal_id': '93041c32866741ec', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'BLUF: The OSS Is Back — In Name. The Hard Part Is the Authorities. <p><em>Secretary of War Pete Hegseth has given the Pentagon’s top special operations civilian the most storied name in American irregular warfare. Whether the new Office of Strategic Services becomes more than a r', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/bluf-the-oss-is-back-in-name-the-hard-part-is-the-authorities'}, {'signal_id': 'fa21eeded4ecf426', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Future of Nvidia Is About More Than AI Chips <p><strong>EXPERT PERSPECTIVE</strong> — Nvidia’s board announced that Jensen Huang had resigned 33 years after he co-founded the company.</p><p>What happens to a company when a visionary CEO is gone? Too often, innovation fades an', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-future-of-nvidia-is-about-more-than-ai-chips'}, {'signal_id': '96a3193ca4c5d5de', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'What\'s Holding Back America\'s Drone Revolution? <img src="https://www.thecipherbrief.com/media-library/drone-in-flight-barre-vt.jpg?id=68708234&amp;width=1245&amp;height=700&amp;coordinates=0%2C52%2C0%2C53" /><br /><br /><p><em>Editorial note: This is the third in a three-part se', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/what-s-holding-back-america-s-drone-revolution'}, {'signal_id': '48b833dea4646c06', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'AI Is Not the Danger. The Vacuum Is. <p>Congress has come back after the midterms for a short lame-duck session, and it has left artificial intelligence where it found it. It had every reason to act. In July, OpenAI disclosed that its AI agents had escaped a testing sandbox and b', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/ai-is-not-the-danger-the-vacuum-is'}, {'signal_id': '3a28a8097842dba5', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The Pentagon Has an AI Strategy. What It Needs Is a Field Guide. <p>OPINION -- Picture a program manager at the Pentagon with money to spend and a job to do: buy an AI tool that helps analysts summarize intelligence reporting. She has read the Defense Department's five ethical pr", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-pentagon-has-an-ai-strategy-what-it-needs-is-a-field-guide'}, {'signal_id': '9f431fb46e59359a', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'America Invented the Drone War, So Why Is It Falling Behind? <img src="https://www.thecipherbrief.com/media-library/a-general-atomics-mq-9-reaper-unmanned-aerial-vehicle-of-the-usaf-is-displayed-on-the-tarmac-during-the-paris-air-show-2025-at-l.jpg?id=68699143&amp;width=1245&amp;', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/america-invented-the-drone-war-so-why-is-it-falling-behind'}, {'signal_id': '7a2e7becfd77e2ff', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "Where Did the Billions From Venezuela's Oil Go? <p>“We've won Venezuela and [have] taken out billions and billions and billions of dollars already. And we will be taking out many billions of dollars and get along very well. And -- you could call it a territory, you could call it ", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/where-did-the-billions-from-venezuela-s-oil-go'}, {'signal_id': '9fc32919e51bc44d', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Reluctant Revolution in Military Affairs (Pt 1) <img src="https://www.thecipherbrief.com/media-library/caption-lviv-ukraine-march-21-2026-fpv-drone-at-the-art-installation-with-anti-drone-nets-in-the-city-center-of-lviv.jpg?id=68692282&amp;width=1245&amp;height=700&amp;coordi', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-reluctant-revolution-in-military-affairs-pt-1'}, {'signal_id': 'ceb66e3d15dfd137', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "America's Autonomous Warfare Command Needs More Than a Name <p>In April 1980, Navy helicopters flown by Marine pilots set out to meet Air Force transports carrying Army assaulters at a strip in the Iranian desert called Desert One. Eight servicemen died there. The review that fol", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-charter-we-must-write'}, {'signal_id': '3282c5e14418f721', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'A Successful Space Race Needs More than “Competitive Supremacy” <p><strong>The final frontier must be mutually beneficial for both US and Allies to be sustainable </strong></p><p>While the demand for digital sovereignty continues to accelerate, driven by geopolitics and strategic', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/a-successful-space-race-needs-more-than-competitive-supremacy'}, {'signal_id': '32ca5cd7b84c5925', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Beijing Holds the Keys to the Drone Wars <p>Welcome to The Iron Triangle, the Cipher Brief column serving Procurement Officers tasked with buying the future, Investors funding the next generation of defense technology, and the Policy Wonks analyzing its impact on the global order', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/one-parts-bin-three-wars-beijing-built-a-valve-we-built-a-wall'}, {'signal_id': 'a483b0a7e159de9d', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Iran Is Poking The Bear <p>Tehran has been playing a dangerous game of chicken with the U.S. administration for months. With the just concluded midterms now in hand, they risk making a dangerous miscalculation just when it matters most. This is unlikely to end well.</p><p>With th', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/iran-is-poking-the-bear'}, {'signal_id': 'c2680ed5349c7fd7', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Year Moscow Felt the War <p>In Moscow this year, people stopped answering “How are you?” with “Fine.” They started saying, “I’m full tank.”</p><p>K. first heard it from a friend, right after drones hit <a href="https://www.adn.com/nation-world/2026/07/01/ukrainian-drone-attac', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-year-moscow-felt-the-war'}, {'signal_id': '65bf48e750c6bfa8', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "What Russia, China, Iran and North Korea Saw in America's Elections <p>Democracy was on display during the 2026 midterm elections in the U.S. Over 124 million ballots were cast across the country, with considerable foreign interest.</p><p>This was democracy in action. A testament", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/what-russia-china-iran-and-north-korea-saw-in-america-s-elections'}, {'signal_id': '80e161497350eda0', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Reinventing Intelligence To Operate At Machine Speed <p>For almost a decade, the U.S. Intelligence Community (IC) has lived with a quiet anxiety: that the proliferation of open-source information, machine learning, and artificial intelligence would one day reshape its analytic en', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/reinventing-intelligence-to-operate-at-machine-speed'}, {'signal_id': '81044c7171d2b5e2', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "What Congress Can Learn From Vietnam About the War in Iran <p>“The American people don't know what the heck we're fighting for in Iran. He's [President Trump] never made it clear. He changes his mind day-to-day and minute-to-minute. This war must end. It must end. And make no mis", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/what-congress-can-learn-from-vietnam-about-the-war-in-iran'}, {'signal_id': 'c2a0899112d2e5b7', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Startups Are Now on the Front Lines <p>A recent Air Force contract to help screen small businesses applying for federal research funding reflects a growing national security concern: foreign access to American innovation.</p><p>Screening applicants is one part of that challenge. ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/startups-are-now-on-the-front-lines'}, {'signal_id': 'aa40e1848e011417', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The Command We Must Fund <p>The Army's Armored Force was born in July 1940, a few weeks after France fell. No act of Congress created it, and no budget line funded it. The Chief of Staff ordered it into being, took the tanks from the infantry and the cavalry, and placed them unde", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-command-we-must-fund'}, {'signal_id': '1758759ee05ab6ab', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "China's Return to One-Man Rule <p>The U.S. will be holding mid-term elections on November 3, to elect the people’s representatives to enact laws, provide oversight and represent the people. In sharp contrast, China’s ruling Communist Party (CCP) announced that it formally expelle", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/china-return-one-man-rule'}, {'signal_id': 'cc09cf691ef60abd', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'In Its Race to Field AI, The Pentagon’s Testing Can’t Keep Up <p><a href="https://www.cnn.com/2026/09/18/politics/us-military-ai-false-intelligence-china-ship" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">CNN reported</a>, citing four sources familiar with the episode, that the U.S.', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/in-its-race-to-field-ai-the-pentagons-testing-cant-keep-up'}, {'signal_id': 'cfcda2cedd54f15b', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Missing Dimension of Cyber Preparedness <p>The technical aspect of incident response can be immense. In extreme scenarios, such as the NotPetya incident in 2017, global organisations such as the shipping company Maersk found the speed and scale of the malware’s impact to be u', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-missing-dimension-of-cyber-preparedness'}, {'signal_id': 'd0688fd3517345b9', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "BLUF: The Next AI Problem for Intelligence Is Not the Model, It's the Manager <p>The Intelligence Community has decided AI agents are coming. It has not decided how they will be supervised, checked and held to analytic standards. In April, CIA Deputy Director Michael Ellis said a", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/bluf-the-next-ai-problem-for-intelligence-is-not-the-model-it-s-the-manager'}, {'signal_id': 'b0f661e1d265e2e1', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Fire Base Australia: Can America’s Southern Base Sustain a Pacific War? <p>American access to Australian bases is only as valuable as Australia’s ability to keep them operating under attack. For Washington, <a href="https://www.defence.gov.au/defence-activities/programs-initiativ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/fire-base-australia-can-americas-southern-base-sustain-a-pacific-war'}, {'signal_id': '2636724d659b320b', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Coming Age of Robotic Warfare <img src="https://www.thecipherbrief.com/media-library/france-defence-army-weaponry.jpg?id=68580393&amp;width=1245&amp;height=700&amp;coordinates=0%2C53%2C0%2C54" /><br /><br /><p>A battalion of armed robots moves against a unit of soldiers, aimi', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-coming-age-of-robotic-warfare'}, {'signal_id': 'e23071c10fb2f7e7', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Hidden Cost of America’s War With Iran <p>“The [U.S. Naval Support Activity Bahrain] base and Fifth Fleet headquarters have been rendered largely inoperable for their original functions, with repairs estimated at $400 million… Chief of Naval Operations Admiral Daryl Caudle an', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/hidden-cost-war-with-iran'}, {'signal_id': 'dd10d7b644f8a031', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Command We Must Start <p><strong></strong>In 1928, Secretary of War Dwight Davis ordered the Army to assemble an experimental mechanized force of tanks, armored cars, and motorized infantry at Camp Meade, Maryland. It was disbanded within months. A second attempt was dissolve', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-command-we-must-start'}, {'signal_id': '43f6f5be3435ac91', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Cipher Brief’s 10th Threat Conference: Optimism, Urgency, and the Imperative to Act <p>Which came first: The Cloister at Sea Island, the Office of Strategic Services, or the CIA? The resort wins. The Cloister first opened in 1928, fourteen years before the OSS and nineteen be', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-cipher-briefs-10th-threat-conference-optimism-urgency-and-the-imperative-to-act'}, {'signal_id': '6114ee09bd6fceae', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Kids are Alright: U.S. Soft Power, Aid, and Youth in Africa <p><em>OPINION — A recent survey of African youth challenges conventional wisdom on foreign aid. Policymakers should take heed of their views as they design the future of U.S. foreign assistance to increase effective', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-kids-are-alright'}, {'signal_id': '306413ae5fced281', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Milestone Crossed: 1,000 Cases Filed Against Trump Administration Policies <p>Charts show different success rates for plaintiffs and the federal government.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/165130/1000-litigation-cases-trump-administration/">Milestone Crossed', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/165130/1000-litigation-cases-trump-administration/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=1000-litigation-cases-trump-administration'}, {'signal_id': '940f3ecc1f491b74', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Bukele’s Troops in Haiti: The Frontlines of an Eroding Rules-Based Global Order? <p>The deployment of thousands of Salvadoran troops to Haiti entrenches a security model in the country beyond legal constraints and U.N. guardrails.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/165102/bukeles-troops-haiti-eroding-rules-based-order/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=bukeles-troops-haiti-eroding-rules-based-order'}, {'signal_id': '821cd3132b12c211', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Remarks of Judge Kimberly Prost at ABILA’s International Law Weekend <p>In her remarks at ABILA\'s International Law Weekend, Judge Kimberly Prost spoke of the resilience of international legal institutions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/164428/remarks-judg', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/164428/remarks-judge-kimberly-prost-abila-international-law-weekend/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=remarks-judge-kimberly-prost-abila-international-law-weekend'}, {'signal_id': '8f11485867739d4d', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Afghanistan’s 80 Years at the U.N.: Keeping the Torch in Times of Darkness <p>The Taliban represents an aberration in Afghanistan\'s long history of living up to its international obligations. The international community must not normalize its rule.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https:', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/164970/afghanistans-80-years-united-nations/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=afghanistans-80-years-united-nations'}, {'signal_id': '798036d1115eada1', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Early Edition: November 19, 2026 <p>Sign up to receive the Early Edition in your inbox\xa0here. A curated weekday guide to major news and developments over the last 24 hours. Here’s today’s news: IRAN WAR President Trump today said the United States would “see what happens” in the I', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/165250/early-edition-november-19-2026/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=early-edition-november-19-2026'}, {'signal_id': '6c0e9dcbc1d38cfa', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'A Series on the Occasion of ABILA’s International Law Weekend 2026 <p>This series explores the theme of this year\'s International Law Weekend, “[R]evolution in the International Legal Order."</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/157835/abila-ilw-2026-series/">A S', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/157835/abila-ilw-2026-series/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=abila-ilw-2026-series'}, {'signal_id': 'f3a2d19a784de9f9', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Litigation Tracker: Case Status Key and Glossary <p>This guide explains how to read each case status in Just Security’s Litigation Tracker and how to interpret a given ruling’s effect on the challenged executive action.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/161783', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/161783/litigation-tracker-case-status-key-glossary/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=litigation-tracker-case-status-key-glossary'}, {'signal_id': '71251dc4c0815961', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Litigation Tracker: Legal Challenges to Trump Administration Actions <p>A public resource tracking all the legal challenges to the Trump administration\'s executive orders and actions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/107087/tracker-litigation-legal-challenges', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/107087/tracker-litigation-legal-challenges-trump-administration/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=tracker-litigation-legal-challenges-trump-administration'}, {'signal_id': '5669882304aae4d3', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'The International Court of Justice Finds that Myanmar Committed Genocide Against the Rohingya: A Preliminary Analysis <p>Analysis of the International Court of Justice\'s judgment in <i>The Gambia v. Myanmar</i> on genocide.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/16', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/165228/icj-judgment-gambia-myanmar-genocide/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=icj-judgment-gambia-myanmar-genocide'}, {'signal_id': '9bfbc454c3f12970', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Guantanamo Dispatches: USS Cole Bombing Trial Recesses With First 8 Jury Members Chosen <p>The latest from Carol Rosenberg on the capital trial at Guantanamo.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/165176/guantanamo-uss-cole-jury/">Guantanamo Dispatches: USS Cole B', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/165176/guantanamo-uss-cole-jury/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=guantanamo-uss-cole-jury'}, {'signal_id': '829372a1c3fc8e60', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Will Teens Just Stay Up Later If School Starts Later? California Says No. Every time a school district considers a later start time, the same objection surfaces: teens will just stay up later. It's an understandable worry. But now we have national data that suggest otherwise.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/11/will-teens-just-stay-up-later-if-school-starts-later.html'}, {'signal_id': '7511ada3869cbc10', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Veterans, Families, and Life After Military Service: Q&amp;A with RAND Experts For veterans, leaving the U.S. military can open new doors and raise new questions. In this Q&amp;A, Carrie Farmer and Rajeev Ramchand share what RAND's research reveals about life after military servi", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/11/veterans-families-and-life-after-military-service-qa.html'}, {'signal_id': '699151b3a720c899', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'Preparedness for the AI Era Requires a Reserve of Critical Workers If governments or employers assume that permanent AI automation is right around the corner, vital training and career pipelines could collapse. We could find ourselves without enough people to perform work essenti', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/11/preparedness-for-the-ai-era-requires-a-reserve-of-critical.html'}, {'signal_id': '2a2e2626dbe7e57d', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Lessons from L.A. on Transfer Taxes San Francisco voters have a new proposition on real estate transfer taxes to consider. Aspects of and arguments for the new Prop 1 closely mirror the debate over Los Angeles' Measure ULA, a 2022 ballot initiative that established a similar tran", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/11/lessons-from-la-on-transfer-taxes.html'}, {'signal_id': 'fa820f34bcc199f0', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Why Employers Can't Tame Health Costs Price transparency alone isn’t helping employers rein in health care costs. What will it take to give them real leverage—and overcome the barriers of today’s system?", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/11/why-employers-cant-tame-health-costs.html'}, {'signal_id': '27c968e09255c3ca', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "America's Least Bad Option in Iran In Iran, the United States could return to a full-scale bombing campaign, walk away from the conflict, or stick with the current approach. Staying the course almost certainly will not bring quick results but it is strategically prudent.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/americas-least-bad-option-in-iran.html'}, {'signal_id': '1360f15fbaf3d074', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Why Quick Compensation Hasn't Replaced Eaton Fire Lawsuits—So Far A review of Southern California Edison's direct-payment program finds that it has paid claimants much faster, but it hasn't become a broad substitute for lawsuits.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/why-quick-compensation-hasnt-replaced-eaton-fire-lawsuits.html'}, {'signal_id': 'b8e2180ad066e052', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'The Missing Link in Drug Policy: Why Whole-System Reform Is Stalling The UK has made progress toward a whole-system approach to drug policy, but unclear accountability and persistent stigma are stalling reform.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/the-missing-link-in-drug-policy-why-whole-system-reform.html'}, {'signal_id': '1c27b342495b14b7', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "A Better Way to Use Criminal Records in Hiring Employers want to know whether an applicant is likely to commit another crime, possibly on the job. But the screening rules many of them use are often about as accurate as a coin toss, in part because they're based on data that don't", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/a-better-way-to-use-criminal-records-in-hiring.html'}, {'signal_id': '7eb450727724ee69', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "This Is How to End Israel's Isolation The hope of many Israelis and Israel's supporters around the world is that elections on Oct. 27 will usher in a new government and slow the slide into greater isolation. New leadership could ease Israel's isolation temporarily. But will a dee", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/this-is-how-to-end-israels-isolation.html'}, {'signal_id': '1f82f8da9de912b0', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Biosecurity in the Age of AI: Q&amp;A with Steph Guerra The question that drives Steph Guerra's work at RAND may be one of the most consequential for this moment in the AI era: How can we harness the full potential of AI for science and medicine—but also ensure it never helps any", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/biosecurity-in-the-age-of-ai-qa-with-steph-guerra.html'}, {'signal_id': '510596eafa31042f', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'From Strategic Logic to Practical Implementation: A Phased Agenda for U.S.-ROK Shipbuilding Cooperation U.S.-ROK cooperation on shipbuilding should be structured so that it strengthens U.S. maritime industrial capacity, makes commercial sense for Korean shipbuilders, and survives', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/from-strategic-logic-to-practical-implementation-a.html'}, {'signal_id': 'c5904b48ce512115', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "9/11's Forgotten Lesson Twenty-five years later, 9/11's lessons are still contested, except the simplest: the United States mistook quiet for peace. And it is doing so again.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/911s-forgotten-lesson.html'}, {'signal_id': '645e5c8159c45b3c', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'Schools, Cell Phones, and AI: Q&amp;A with Melissa Kay Diliberti Melissa Kay Diliberti, an associate policy researcher at RAND, discusses recent findings from RAND that can help parents and policymakers better understand what challenges schools are up against.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/schools-cell-phones-and-ai-qa-with-melissa-kay-diliberti.html'}, {'signal_id': 'f0a6bf01926bc40a', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Netanyahu May Have Ignored a Dire Warning. Israel Ignores the Deeper Threat. Israel's strategy in Gaza is only keeping Hamas in power: deterred, but not replaced, with no real alternative given a chance. A different outcome calls for a different approach.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/nentanyahu-may-have-ignored-a-dire-warning-israel-ignores-the.html'}, {'signal_id': 'b489a15858be84c1', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Never Underestimate the Houthis Yemen's Houthi rebels are in a position to shape the next phase of the conflict between the United States and Iran if they attempt to renew their blockade of the Bab al-Mandab Strait. And no one should assume that a deal with Iran will bind what th", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/never-underestimate-the-houthis.html'}, {'signal_id': '19d8064c433770cf', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Preserving Jobs and Tax Revenue in the Age of AI: Q&amp;A with Carter Price Carter Price, a mathematician at RAND and co-director of the RAND Von Furstenberg Family Budget Model Initiative, discusses ways to rebalance the tax code so that it doesn't incentivize employers to repla", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/preserving-jobs-and-tax-revenue-in-the-age-of-ai-qa.html'}, {'signal_id': 'd2d02311d1d9e0e7', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'The Recent Rise of Women Gun Owners In recent years, women made up almost half of all new gun owners, a striking shift from the historical norm, when women accounted for about a quarter of them. And the uptick is widespread across geographic and demographic subgroups.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/the-recent-rise-of-women-gun-owners.html'}, {'signal_id': '2a9dc8988cf7146c', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Who Benefits from Education Savings Accounts? Q&amp;A with Susha Roy Tens of thousands of American families use state-funded education savings accounts for their children's education. How exactly do these accounts work? Who benefits from them? And how do they affect education fun", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/who-benefits-from-education-savings-accounts.html'}, {'signal_id': '480b7da85115059d', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Getting a Security Clearance Doesn't Have to Be So Intimidating: Q&amp;A with Sina Beaghley The security clearance process can be difficult and time-consuming but the government has made big strides in improving it. Sina Beaghley, a senior international and defense researcher at ", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/getting-a-security-clearance-doesnt-have-to-be-so-intimidating.html'}, {'signal_id': 'e10bdbdebdb50e0c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Putin didn’t get his Yalta, but he’s happy nonetheless <p>In the Shenzhen summit with Trump and Xi, Putin got the propaganda victory he wanted without having to make any concessions on Ukraine.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/putin-didnt-get-hi', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/putin-didnt-get-his-yalta-but-hes-happy-nonetheless/'}, {'signal_id': '3acc719f46a23dd5', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What the Trump-Putin-Xi meeting actually achieved <p>Our experts unpack what Trump, Xi, and Putin gained from their summit and what their declaration means for the global order.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-the-trump-pu', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-the-trump-putin-xi-meeting-actually-achieved/'}, {'signal_id': 'be9ce391270a0dbc', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The US didn’t have a strong plan for the Shenzhen summit. It showed. <p>The leaders’ trilateral meeting in Shenzhen ended up benefiting Beijing and Moscow at the expense of Washington.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/the-us-didnt-have-a-strong-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/the-us-didnt-have-a-strong-plan-for-the-shenzhen-summit-it-showed/'}, {'signal_id': 'cf5fbe10bf1a7c2c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for The Jerusalem Strategic Tribune: The Hidden Cost of America’s Political Inconsistency <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-the-hidden-cost-of-americas-political-inconsistency/">Charai', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-the-hidden-cost-of-americas-political-inconsistency/'}, {'signal_id': '9c32d299dc73844b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lessons from Brazil and Peru on how to build AI-ready institutions across Latin America <p>Brazil and Peru offer early blueprints for AI regulation in Latin America: one for building regulatory institutions before legislation is in place, and another for turning AI laws into effe', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/geotech-cues/lessons-from-brazil-and-peru-on-how-to-build-ai-ready-institutions-across-latin-america/'}, {'signal_id': 'e5abd59fe48093c4', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from Manama: The Iran war is not over for Bahrain <p>A recent visit to Bahrain offers a window into the ongoing tensions with Iran and diplomatic maneuvering among Gulf nations.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/dispatch-from-manama-the-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/dispatch-from-manama-the-most-underappreciated-us-ally-in-the-gulf/'}, {'signal_id': 'bc7674d1a96ddd0d', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Kyiv’s partners should prioritize Ukraine’s domestic drone production <p>Ukrainian long-range drone strikes have reduced Russian oil refining output by around 45 percent in the past few weeks, Reuters reports. Kyiv's partners should build on this success and prioritize funding fo", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/kyivs-partners-should-prioritize-ukraines-domestic-drone-production/'}, {'signal_id': '196459d639fde4fb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'US Energy Secretary Chris Wright and Polish Energy Minister Miłosz Motyka on why Europe’s security depends on its energy supply <p>The two energy leaders spoke at the seventh Partnership for Transatlantic Energy Cooperation in Warsaw.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlantic', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/news/transcripts/us-energy-secretary-chris-wright-and-polish-energy-minister-milosz-motyka-on-why-europes-security-depends-on-its-energy-supply/'}, {'signal_id': '50f7a50fbec9420e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Five European ministers on why they won’t go back to business with Russia <p>Economy and energy ministers from across Central and Eastern Europe warned at the Partnership for Transatlantic Energy Cooperation that Europe can't fall back on cheap energy that will be used as a polit", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/event-recap/five-european-ministers-on-why-they-wont-go-back-to-business-with-russia/'}, {'signal_id': '837e4f78f507a9f5', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The foresight brief: Chokepoints past, present, and future <p>Maritime straits, canals, ports, rivers, subsea cables, data centers, and cloud infrastructure are concentrated points of connection. Yet their significance is changing as supply chains evolve, geopolitical competition', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/the-foresight-brief-chokepoints-past-present-and-future/'}, {'signal_id': '54393727c04e5c46', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Mercenaries, apps, and crypto: Russia’s hybrid war on Europe <p>Alia Brahimi and Alexander Kolyandr discuss the “one-shot” mercenaries Russia employs for its shadow war in Europe.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/podcast/mercenaries-apps-and-cry', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/podcast/mercenaries-apps-and-crypto-russias-hybrid-war-on-europe/'}, {'signal_id': 'adeadcbdc18014a8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Toplines: Why and how the United States and its allies should prepare for a limited nuclear attack <p>How should the United States and its allies prepare for a limited nuclear attack, and why? An expert tabletop exercise gaming out scenarios in which North Korea might launch such', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/toplines-why-and-how-the-united-states-and-its-allies-should-prepare-for-a-limited-nuclear-attack/'}, {'signal_id': 'd56011b08b831d4f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Estonia has a chance to reboot the Ukraine Recovery Conference <p>The 2027 Ukraine Recovery Conference in Tallinn is an opportunity to turn this event from a one-off series of signing ceremonies into a substantive discussion of Ukraine’s future, writes Luke Zahner.</p>\n<p>The pos', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/estonia-has-a-chance-to-reboot-the-ukraine-recovery-conference/'}, {'signal_id': '762222bdcb0733c6', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Donald Tusk, Chris Wright, and Miłosz Motyka on the mindset shift needed across the energy system <p>The three leaders spoke at the seventh Partnership for Transatlantic Energy Cooperation, making the case for more energy production as supplies tighten and prices skyrocket.</p>\n<', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/event-recap/donald-tusk-chris-wright-and-milosz-motyka-on-the-mindset-shift-needed-across-the-energy-system/'}, {'signal_id': '8037c2c328bd7d40', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Libya’s reunification and path to democracy start with fixing its budget <p>A recent Atlantic Council roundtable with Libyan officials, Italian policymakers, and international experts and analysts examined UN and US efforts to reunite the country.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https:/', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/libyas-reunification-and-path-to-democracy-start-with-fixing-its-budget/'}, {'signal_id': '8c26e3d89b5eceda', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from Kyiv: Let Ukraine strike Russia’s missile launchers at the source <p>Russia\'s missile production vastly outpaces the output of interceptors for Ukraine and by the United States—an issue that should concern militaries around the world.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https:', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/dispatch-from-kyiv-let-ukraine-strike-russias-missile-launchers-at-the-source/'}, {'signal_id': '75003983b81ed676', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Upheaval in the Greater North African Security Complex demands a new transatlantic policy approach <p>A recent Atlantic Council roundtable brought together Italian policymakers, international experts, and analysts to examine interconnected security dynamics across North Africa, t', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/upheaval-in-the-greater-north-african-security-complex-demands-a-new-transatlantic-policy-approach/'}, {'signal_id': '4b63716df156425f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lichfield cited in a The Diplomatic Insight article on Trump’s Russian diesel deal and congressional opposition <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliabi', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-9-6/'}, {'signal_id': '852f732170f69cb5', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lichfield quoted in CNN on the impact of the Russian sanctions waiver on US importers <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lichfield-quoted-in-cnn-on-the-impact-of-the-russian-sanctions-waiver-on-us-impo', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lichfield-quoted-in-cnn-on-the-impact-of-the-russian-sanctions-waiver-on-us-importers/'}, {'signal_id': '53b3718f09b340e1', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lipsky quoted in Bloomberg on Trump’s trade leverage ahead of the Xi summit <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-bloomberg-on-trumps-trade-leverage-ahead-of-the-xi-summit/">Lipsky quoted', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-bloomberg-on-trumps-trade-leverage-ahead-of-the-xi-summit/'}, {'signal_id': '1fb6c95f6c8a3564', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'In Shenzhen, weakened giants navigate a dangerous, disorderly world <p>When the US, Russian, and Chinese presidents meet on Thursday, weakness rather than strength may prove the most consequential force.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/infl', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/in-shenzhen-weakened-giants-navigate-a-dangerous-disorderly-world/'}, {'signal_id': '6a758a7db039d026', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Russia’s colossal losses in Ukraine will not push Putin toward peace <p>Russia\'s heavy losses in Ukraine may hamper Putin’s invasion, but they will not push the Kremlin dictator toward the negotiating table, writes David Kirichenko.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticco', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/russias-colossal-losses-in-ukraine-will-not-push-putin-toward-peace/'}, {'signal_id': '474f3b6b0f75e81c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Ukraine’s Crimean Bridge attack is a very personal humiliation for Putin <p>Ukraine hit and partially destroyed the Crimean Bridge on November 17 with an unprecedented drone and missile strike that highlighted Russia's vulnerabilities and served as a very personal humiliation for", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraines-crimean-bridge-attack-is-a-very-personal-humiliation-for-putin/'}, {'signal_id': '630eeba32fd365bb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Positive economic statecraft in a fractured world: ASEAN in focus <p>Positive economic statecraft (PES) was conceptualized in a macro and geoeconomic landscape that has changed considerably.  </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issu', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/positive-economic-statecraft-in-a-fractured-world/'}, {'signal_id': '5dff2367136e9a42', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'As the Nvidia scandal threatens to reignite trade tensions at Trump-Xi talks, Beijing still holds the rare earths <p>Washington’s push to close loopholes could invite renewed Chinese restrictions on rare earths, exposing a supply-chain vulnerability that the trade truce never res', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/as-the-nvidia-scandal-threatens-to-reignite-trade-tensions-at-trump-xi-talks-beijing-still-holds-the-rare-earths/'}, {'signal_id': '8b9e12ceb8c4dd7b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What Trump, Putin, and Xi want from their meeting in Shenzhen <p>Atlantic Council experts answer seven pressing questions ahead of the meeting of the US, Russia, and Chinese presidents.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-trump-putin-and-xi-wa', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-trump-putin-and-xi-want-from-their-meeting-in-shenzhen/'}, {'signal_id': 'ea7413edbb6d3dd3', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Spain votes first: What its snap election could mean for Europe and the United States <p>With nationalist parties gaining ground across Europe, Sánchez’s record offers a warning about the limits of mobilizing voters against them.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcounc', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/spain-votes-first-what-its-snap-election-could-mean-for-europe-and-the-united-states/'}, {'signal_id': '88e0c0158bf43f42', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Congress could soon rein in Trump’s tariffs on Canada. Here’s what that could look like. <p>Removing Section 338 tariffs on Canada may be a good place to start for the new Congress.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/congress-could-soon-r', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/congress-could-soon-rein-in-trumps-tariffs-on-canada-heres-what-that-could-look-like/'}, {'signal_id': 'a9e5c8d35a118002', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'AI agents promise a life free from friction. The cost could be human judgment. <p>Artificial intelligence can create a false sense of certainty for users by delivering fluent answers without noting uncertainty or the reasoning behind responses.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://ww', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/ai-agents-promise-a-life-free-from-friction-the-cost-could-be-human-judgment/'}, {'signal_id': '18b98916db60f143', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Why Venezuela’s oil recovery depends on fixing its natural gas market <p>Venezuela has vast natural gas reserves, yet flares or vents half of what it produces. The core failure is market design, not the law.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-resear', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/why-venezuelas-oil-recovery-depends-on-fixing-its-natural-gas-market/'}, {'signal_id': '74f5611b66222bb2', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Thirty years of progress, lost at sea <p>The oceans are more dangerous now than at any time in the thirty years since the UN Convention on the Law of the Sea was signed. And it's not just the Strait of Hormuz: Attacks on civilian merchant shipping are now common in the Persian Gu", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/thirty-years-of-progress-lost-at-sea/'}, {'signal_id': '40d74b5a1ac160ee', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Why Congress and the European Parliament need an AI safety dialogue <p>While talks at the executive level would be welcome, the next steps on AI safety may well come from US and European legislators.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/why-congress', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/why-congress-and-the-european-parliament-need-an-ai-safety-dialogue/'}, {'signal_id': '15a4ebb1f1c8c41b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Can Montenegro’s accession reinvigorate EU enlargement? A Debrief with Gert Jan Koopman <p>Europe Center Resident Senior Fellow Ilva Tare speaks with Director-General Gert Jan Koopman, the European Commission's Director-General for Enlargement and Eastern Neighbourhood, about EU ", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/balkans-debrief/can-montenegros-accession-reinvigorate-eu-enlargement-a-debrief-with-gert-jan-koopman/'}, {'signal_id': '1c1a40f1288ba0ea', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The rising cost of ambition in Saudi Arabia’s Vision 2030 <p>The Iran war and the rising cost of global capital demand a reassessment of the assumptions underlying how Vision 2030 is executed.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/the-rising-co', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/the-rising-cost-of-ambition-in-saudi-arabias-vision-2030/'}, {'signal_id': '69ad14370f75dcf7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "A new vision for the Vertical Corridor: European energy security through infrastructure optimization <p>Europe's Vertical Corridor region is well positioned to reverse its historical Soviet infrastructure legacy and natural gas dependency, while supporting broader European energy", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/a-new-vision-for-the-vertical-corridor-european-energy-security-through-infrastructure-optimization/'}, {'signal_id': '7d5495f668de48e1', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Syria shouldn’t join the Mecca Alliance. It should cooperate with it. <p>Joining the alliance would expose Syria to a new set of threats and increase the chances of regional escalation.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/syria-shouldnt-join-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/syria-shouldnt-join-the-mecca-alliance-it-should-cooperate-with-it/'}, {'signal_id': '94339e681ed70c3a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "The election that never happened, and why Washington needs a new strategy toward Nicaragua <p>Nicaragua's dictators called for no more elections, so Washington should call for no more business as usual. It should use targeted economic pressure to push for democratic change. </p>\n", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/the-election-that-never-happened-and-why-washington-needs-a-new-strategy-toward-nicaragua/'}, {'signal_id': '29a4179389f8832f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Same metric, still a mess: The geoeconomics of youth unemployment in China <p>China is aging too quickly to waste labor, yet it can\'t generate enough jobs to productively engage its young.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/same-metric-st', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/same-metric-still-a-mess-the-geoeconomics-of-youth-unemployment-in-china/'}, {'signal_id': 'b8cd85cdb1281ec8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Washington is reshaping security in North Africa. Congress needs to ask how. <p>The next US Congress should demand clearer plans from the White House on its Western Sahara and Libya policies. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/washington-is', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/washington-is-reshaping-security-in-north-africa-congress-needs-to-ask-how/'}, {'signal_id': '04131853efe1af1e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lichfield interviewed on Bloomberg TV to discuss Nvidia’s leadership crisis and the US – China AI competition <p>Watch the full interview here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliab', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-9-5/'}, {'signal_id': 'fc4f52a61ae620fb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lichfield and de Kruijf cited in a CNN on the dynamic between Russia and the Trump administration <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influenci', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-9-4/'}, {'signal_id': '02c2db871789b7da', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lichfield quoted in a Reuters on the midterm impact on the US support for Ukraine and policy towards Russia <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-9-3/'}, {'signal_id': 'acf993019416de8e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Tuteja interviewed on Bloomberg Tech about the implications of the midterm elections for data center development and the AI regulation <p>Watch the full interview here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-9-2/'}, {'signal_id': '8f2ea2a328203288', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Putin’s chief negotiator vows to seize ‘every inch of Russian land’ in Ukraine <p>The Kremlin’s uncompromising approach to negotiations with Ukraine was summed up by Russian delegation head Vladimir Medinsky's comment that “every inch of Russian land will be returned to Russia, o", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/putins-chief-negotiator-vows-to-return-every-inch-of-russian-land-in-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': '6a462563b9fe9f17', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Moldova cuts energy dependency on Russia with landmark new power line <p>Five years after Russia tried to bring Moldova to its knees through energy pressure, a landmark new power line has removed one of Moscow’s last remaining levers over the country, writes Aura Sabadus.</p>\n<p>', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/moldova-cuts-energy-dependency-on-russia-with-landmark-new-power-line/'}, {'signal_id': '4257c27800b8e41d', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The digital yuan is only part of China’s expanding global payments network <p>Beijing is building multiple layers of financial infrastructure to engage more partners and expand the reach of its renminbi.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/the-digital-yuan-is-only-part-of-chinas-expanding-global-payments-network/'}, {'signal_id': '40e6aab2859e46d5', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What Jensen Huang’s Nvidia exit means for Washington, Wall Street, and Beijing <p>Our experts unpack what the alleged Nvidia espionage incident means for national security, markets, and relations with Beijing.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-serie', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-jensen-huangs-nvidia-exit-means-for-washington-wall-street-and-beijing/'}, {'signal_id': '8d70408a2a3bb52e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Beyond the spy scandal: What the Nvidia-Megaspeed case reveals about export controls <p>Washington must help the private sector protect technology and sensitive information against foreign threats.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/beyond-the-spy', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/beyond-the-spy-scandal-what-the-nvidia-megaspeed-case-reveals-about-export-controls/'}, {'signal_id': '8dae0c362e993115', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Seeking the source: Biological attribution from anthrax to AI <p>Attribution can be imprecise, since it oftentimes relies on a combination of science, intelligence, and investigatory evidence. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/rep', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/seeking-the-source-biological-attribution-from-anthrax-to-ai/'}, {'signal_id': 'f4b89699209b2372', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Where the Russia-Ukraine peace talks stand after Abu Dhabi <p>Our experts unpack what this week’s US-brokered talks between Russia and Ukraine mean for European security and the prospects for peace.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthink', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/where-the-russia-ukraine-peace-talks-stand-after-abu-dhabi/'}, {'signal_id': '7f07370306af947e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Ukraine’s new drone blitz cuts Russian oil refining capacity by 30 percent <p>Ukraine has renewed attacks on Putin's energy industry in recent days, conducting a series of powerful strikes that have reportedly cut Russian oil refining capacity by around 30 percent and sparked fue", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraines-new-drone-blitz-cuts-russian-oil-refining-capacity-by-30-percent/'}, {'signal_id': 'f597f91d3c9e701b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Europe sees surge in suspected Russian hybrid warfare incidents <p>Europe has witnessed a surge in suspected Russian hybrid warfare incidents in recent weeks. This is fueling concerns that Vladimir Putin is escalating his intimidation campaign against Ukraine’s partners, writes M', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/europe-sees-surge-in-suspected-russian-hybrid-warfare-incidents/'}, {'signal_id': '5d9fa876c790088c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Nick Clegg on Trump, Silicon Valley, and Big Tech’s political shift <p>Nick Clegg, former British deputy prime minister and Meta’s former president of global affairs, joins Frederick Kempe for a candid conversation about his time in government.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://ww', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/inflection-points-with-frederick-kempe/nick-clegg-on-trumo-silicon-valley-and-big-techs-political-shift/'}, {'signal_id': '0b707e3489cb71c1', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Materials matter: Managing critical commodities for the next-generation energy economy <p>As economies electrify, demand will grow for materials such as copper, steel, and durable plastics that underpin the energy system. Managing these materials' supply risks will be crucial to ", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/materials-matter-managing-critical-commodities-for-the-next-generation-energy-economy/'}, {'signal_id': 'f0089138a9a025eb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Water infrastructure at the Mediterranean’s inflection point: Financing resilience for an industrializing, digitalizing region <p>Increasing demand, driven by industrialization and digital infrastructure, requires a region-wide rethinking of water planning and financing mechanism', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/water-infrastructure-at-the-mediterraneans-inflection-point/'}, {'signal_id': '3bc53481eefaa84c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What students got right about the $6 billion Binance hack, and how they would prevent the next one <p>A year before the largest cryptocurrency theft in history, students at an Atlantic Council cyber strategy competition encountered an eerily similar scenario.</p>\n<p>The post <a h', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-students-got-right-about-the-6-billion-binance-hack-and-how-they-would-prevent-the-next-one/'}, {'signal_id': '9548d168023b5709', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from Berlin: What Germans most want to know about the post-midterms United States <p>Germany faces even more pressure to lead European security amid uncertainty over the Trump administration\'s post-midterm Russia policy.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcounc', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-germans-most-want-to-know-about-the-post-midterms-united-states/'}, {'signal_id': '703b23f5cba07571', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for The National Interest: On Immigration, the US Is Not Europe—Unless It Chooses to Be <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-national-interest-on-immigration-the-us-is-not-europe-unless-it-chooses-to-be/">Charai for', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-national-interest-on-immigration-the-us-is-not-europe-unless-it-chooses-to-be/'}, {'signal_id': '26a4069e351d54f3', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dollar Dominance Monitor cited in a Project Syndicate article on the yuan’s growing role in international trade <p>Read the article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/the-cbdc-tracker-cited-in-coindesk-on-the-number-of-countri', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/the-cbdc-tracker-cited-in-coindesk-on-the-number-of-countries-actively-testing-or-developing-cbdcs-2-3/'}, {'signal_id': 'df72a58dbbcc7043', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'CBDC Tracker cited in a CEPR paper on Europe’s plans for retail and wholesale payments <p>Read the article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/the-cbdc-tracker-cited-in-coindesk-on-the-number-of-countries-actively-testing-or-de', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/the-cbdc-tracker-cited-in-coindesk-on-the-number-of-countries-actively-testing-or-developing-cbdcs-2-2/'}, {'signal_id': 'c4b562f5ec37fa1b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lipsky and Piasecki quoted in a China Daily article on the impact of the 2027 budget and debt ceiling negotiations on global financial markets <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-9/'}, {'signal_id': '0c2de8dd923e5461', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lichfield interviewed by Radio Télévision Suisse (RTS) about the US midterm elections <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollar', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-8/'}, {'signal_id': '4491c55cffcf71a7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lipsky quoted in a South China Morning Post article discussing how Congress could constrain Trump’s agenda following the 2026 US midterm elections <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-7/'}, {'signal_id': 'edf2ba8bd364e9a1', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chhangani’s article on the future of the digital euro cited in an OMFIF article <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarizatio', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-6/'}, {'signal_id': '7d3727850d11ec4a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lichfield interviewed by France Culture (Radio France) on how Trump’s economic policies could affect Republican support in the 2026 midterm elections <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-5/'}, {'signal_id': '2363667b922201e6', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Piasecki’s research on Venezuela’s debt restructuring cited in a Congressional Research Service report <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-infl', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-4/'}, {'signal_id': 'c781768a129490e2', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chhangani quoted in an AFP article on the G20 foreign ministers’ meeting in Atlanta <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollariz', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-3/'}, {'signal_id': '5a39d271cf3a453f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lipsky quoted in a South China Morning Post article on how Democrats could push to rein in Trump’s tariffs and give Congress more control over trade policy <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-4-2/'}, {'signal_id': 'e6af0cdfa3071acb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from Dubai: After the midterms, allies see both US resilience and unreliability <p>In the Middle East, Europe, and Asia, allies are impressed by US democratic resilience but worried about policy predictability.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/con', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/dispatch-from-dubai-after-the-midterms-allies-see-both-us-resilience-and-unreliability/'}, {'signal_id': 'f051b77c4c916b09', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Why Belgrade’s new government should not let the Vertical Gas Corridor slip <p>Serbia’s incoming government should stay the course on the Vertical Gas Corridor to advance economic growth, energy security, and market transparency in line with the Student List’s reform agenda.</p>\n', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/energysource/why-belgrades-new-government-should-not-let-the-vertical-gas-corridor-slip/'}, {'signal_id': '7ca16578abb7fe5b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Putin wants peace talks. He doesn’t want peace. <p>The Russian president is using negotiations, including the upcoming US-Ukraine-Russia talks in Abu Dhabi, to buy time and extract concessions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/putin-wants-peace-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/putin-wants-peace-talks-he-doesnt-want-peace/'}, {'signal_id': 'e4081afe3420a4a2', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The six strategic mistakes that led to US defeat in Afghanistan <p>Twenty-five years on, the United States\' defeat in Afghanistan appears less inevitable than the result of decisions that undermined its ability to prevent the Taliban\'s resurgence.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https:/', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/the-six-strategic-mistakes-that-led-to-us-defeat-in-afghanistan/'}, {'signal_id': 'aa05b74995a1ec7b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'To settle Russia’s Ukraine war, Europe needs to let Kyiv in. Trump can help (really). <p>Any deal to end the war in Ukraine must fix a date for Kyiv to join the EU, but countless hurdles stand in the way. Washington has the leverage to help Brussels clear them—if it can use that ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/to-settle-russias-ukraine-war-europe-needs-to-let-kyiv-in-trump-can-help-really/'}, {'signal_id': 'd58e68beb3bd8752', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Not quite mercenaries: How Russia lures thousands of foreigners to fight in its war on Ukraine <p>Many of Russia\'s foreign recruits were coerced into service due to vulnerable legal or financial statuses. What should become of them?</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticco', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/not-quite-mercenaries-how-russia-lures-thousands-of-foreigners-to-fight-in-its-war-on-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': '55bf973475fe904f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Putin suffers Balkan setbacks as Russia struggles to retain influence <p>Russia’s recent setbacks in the Balkans are a reminder of the foreign policy challenges facing the Kremlin as the full-scale invasion of Ukraine approaches a sixth year with no end in sight, writes Michael G', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/putin-suffers-balkan-setbacks-as-russia-struggles-to-retain-influence/'}, {'signal_id': 'f6458a64ac188ee9', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Last week’s brief Ukraine ceasefire did not stop Russian attacks on civilians <p>A recent humanitarian ceasefire around the southern Ukrainian city of Oleshky made it possible to evacuate hundreds of residents, but Russian attacks on civilians elsewhere in Ukraine continue, write', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/last-weeks-brief-ukraine-ceasefire-did-not-stop-russian-attacks-on-civilians/'}, {'signal_id': 'e8ab9ff105e60eb4', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Washington should broaden its Shia outreach in Iraq. Muqtada al-Sadr is a case study. <p>Conversations with several Sadrists reveal a movement preparing to fill a leadership vacuum in Iraq—and engage with the US.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/mena', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/washington-should-broaden-its-shia-outreach-in-iraq-muqtada-al-sadr-is-a-case-study/'}, {'signal_id': '30a855686c4c1940', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for The Jerusalem Post: Can Israeli leaders afford not to change after the American midterm results? <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-post-can-israeli-leaders-afford-not-to-change-after-the-american-mi', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-post-can-israeli-leaders-afford-not-to-change-after-the-american-midterm-results/'}, {'signal_id': '64df3e43ad8ae877', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'As Gen Z asserts itself in Serbia and Albania, the upside for the West is far greater than the headaches <p>The West has an opening to advance democratic values and foreign policy alignment in the Balkans.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/as-gen', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/as-gen-z-asserts-itself-in-serbia-and-albania-the-upside-for-the-west-is-far-greater-than-the-headaches/'}, {'signal_id': '0042092f79ca5a88', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Why this US midterm was unusually important for the Middle East <p>Midterm losses may reduce the immediate risk of renewed US strikes on Iran, but could drive Trump toward escalation in the months ahead.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/why-this', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/why-this-us-midterm-was-unusually-important-for-the-middle-east/'}, {'signal_id': 'fd30df6bfedd98f7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What the midterms will (and won’t) change for US foreign policy <p> Our experts explain where the power shift could change foreign policy—and where it won’t.\xa0</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-the-midterms-will-and-wont-chan', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-the-midterms-will-and-wont-change-for-us-foreign-policy/'}, {'signal_id': 'def8585680f48b41', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for The Jerusalem Strategic Tribune: The Midterm Verdict and the Test of American Leadership <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-the-midterm-verdict-and-the-test-of-american-leadership/"', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-the-midterm-verdict-and-the-test-of-american-leadership/'}, {'signal_id': 'c9820844989a7507', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Experts react: Democrats just swept the US midterms. Here’s what it means for the world. <p>Our experts assess the global implications of the midterm elections on issues ranging from energy and the economy to US foreign policy.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/experts-react-democrats-just-swept-the-us-midterms-heres-what-it-means-for-the-world/'}, {'signal_id': 'c3dc3f0c4c083ce7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The midterms are done. Time for the fiscal clashes to begin. <p>The Democrats’ victory in the 2026 US midterm elections sets the stage for major showdowns on the federal budget and the debt ceiling.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/the-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/the-midterms-are-done-time-for-the-fiscal-clashes-to-begin/'}, {'signal_id': '51d418ea744e28a7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'A $6 billion hack in a season of AI anxiety <p>A $6.3 billion Binance hack and AI-assisted discoveries of software vulnerabilities made unsettling headlines. But not everything is as new or terrifying as it seems.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/eco', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/a-6-billion-hack-in-a-season-of-ai-anxiety/'}, {'signal_id': 'ac2e247d95eba903', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Europe must weigh rising Ukraine costs against higher price of Russian victory <p>If Russia succeeds in overrunning an underfunded and exhausted Ukraine, the consequences for Europe will be catastrophic and the price tag of stopping an emboldened Putin will dwarf the current cost', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/europe-must-weigh-rising-cost-of-supporting-ukraine-against-far-higher-price-of-russian-victory/'}, {'signal_id': '9ed1a9e43b8f21a1', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'A strong defense industry may be Ukraine’s best security guarantee <p>Ukrainians have little faith in written guarantees and are well aware that nobody is going to fight Russia on their behalf. Instead, their most realistic security guarantee is a strong Ukrainian military backed', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/a-strong-defense-industry-may-be-ukraines-best-security-guarantee/'}, {'signal_id': '06f47ff5b9196be7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'New Palestinian leaders will need more than an electoral mandate to govern <p>The 2027 Palestinian elections will only give new leaders the authority to govern if they can control finances and security and rival factions agree to accept the results.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/new-palestinian-leaders-will-need-more-than-an-electoral-mandate-to-govern/'}, {'signal_id': '48c0a4431fdad63a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Religion as statecraft: What a decade of research reveals about the geopolitics of religious soft power <p>The post-Cold War assumption that international politics was converging toward a secular liberal framework in which religion would play at most a marginal role has not survi', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/religion-as-statecraft-what-a-decade-of-research-reveals-about-the-geopolitics-of-religious-soft-power/'}, {'signal_id': '2f21c01cb61a67c8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from Abu Dhabi: America votes—and the world holds its breath <p>The world is showing more interest than ever in the US midterm elections, and with good reason given how the results could affect Trump\'s foreign policy.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/dispatch-from-abu-dhabi-america-votes-and-the-world-holds-its-breath/'}, {'signal_id': '5ad7af3ef0557cfc', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Scowcroft Strategy Scorecard: Grading Canada’s second-ever national security strategy <p>For only the second time in its history, Canada has a new national security strategy. Does it match the clarity with which Prime Minister Mark Carney has described the challenges the country ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/scorecard/scowcroft-strategy-scorecard-grading-canadas-second-ever-national-security-strategy/'}, {'signal_id': '305d78c1be93e255', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for The Jerusalem Strategic Tribune: The Iran War: What Victory Must Achieve. <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-the-iran-war-what-victory-must-achieve/">Charai for The Jerusalem Strate', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-the-iran-war-what-victory-must-achieve/'}, {'signal_id': '3f21234d817e4e7a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How to prevent an energy quarantine of Taiwan <p>An all-of-the-above energy strategy in Taiwan can help the United States and allies deter a Chinese energy quarantine of the island.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/how', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/how-to-prevent-an-energy-quarantine-of-taiwan/'}, {'signal_id': '72a3e6dde5a2e9ab', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'As energy prices threaten inflation again, Lagarde’s European Central Bank legacy offers lessons <p>Christine Lagarde\'s European Central Bank legacy reflects strong crisis management and efforts to strengthen the euro, but a mixed record on inflation.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="htt', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/as-energy-prices-threaten-inflation-again-lagardes-european-central-bank-legacy-offers-lessons/'}, {'signal_id': 'c5f106fd0eb26daa', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in Washington Tariff & Trade Letter on the US’s use of Smoot-Hawley law to impose tariffs on Canada <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-washington-tariff-trade-letter-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-washington-tariff-trade-letter-on-the-uss-use-of-smoot-hawley-law-to-impose-tariffs-on-canada/'}, {'signal_id': '8b2a0910ab390025', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in National Post on the implications of USMCA uncertainty on long-term North American supply chain security <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-national-post-on-the-im', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-national-post-on-the-implications-of-usmca-uncertainty-on-long-term-north-american-supply-chain-security/'}, {'signal_id': '5544debd93d9e27e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in Reforma on how China benefits from USMCA uncertainty and fragmentation <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-reforma-on-how-china-benefits-from-usmca-uncertainty-and-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-reforma-on-how-china-benefits-from-usmca-uncertainty-and-fragmentation/'}, {'signal_id': 'd6db05d976be6e1f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in Financial Review on the USMCA renegotiating process and the implications of uncertainty for the trade bloc <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-financial-review-on-t', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-financial-review-on-the-usmca-renegotiating-process-and-the-implications-of-uncertainty-for-the-trade-bloc/'}, {'signal_id': 'fb7557ba434605b2', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chalecki quoted in Barron’s on how Canada’s economy can sustain disruptions and mixed signals on trade from US <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-barrons-on-how-canadas-economy-can-s', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/chalecki-quoted-in-barrons-on-how-canadas-economy-can-sustain-disruptions-and-mixed-signals-on-trade-from-us/'}, {'signal_id': '65c639722093fd44', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Nikoladze quoted in The Christian Science Monitor on the effectiveness of tariffs authorized by the Russia Sanctions Act of 2026 <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/nikoladze-quoted-in-the-christian-sci', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/nikoladze-quoted-in-the-christian-science-monitor-on-the-effectiveness-of-tariffs-authorized-by-the-russia-sanctions-act-of-2026/'}, {'signal_id': '4def9464fa28e599', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Navy will likely fly CCAs sooner than F/A-XX, White House nom says William Toti, who’s been doing the job since May, is up for permanent appointment as Navy undersecretary.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/defense-systems/2026/11/navy-will-likely-fly-ccas-sooner-f-xx-white-house-nom-says/417365/'}, {'signal_id': '2fee16ad3f39d05e', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': "White House fires cyber director in wake of outages, sources say Sean Cairncross is to be replaced by Pentagon's CIO; doubts grow about CISA nominee.", 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/policy/2026/11/pentagon-cio-replaces-white-house-cyber-director-sean-cairncross-major-shakeup/417359/'}, {'signal_id': '1fed2bd44e10b317', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'The Army wants its units to use more data, but many aren’t built to do so AI might help move intelligence more quickly up and down the echelons, Army and industry speakers said.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/technology/2026/11/army-wants-its-units-use-more-data-many-arent-built-do-so/417355/'}, {'signal_id': 'e8233c3048f4d7c6', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': '‘I was seriously wrong’: Experts say superintelligent AI may arrive as soon as next year AI is speeding up research, potentially creating a runaway loop.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/threats/2026/11/i-was-seriously-wrong-ai-experts-say-superintelligent-ai-may-arrive-soon-next-year/417348/'}, {'signal_id': '4a9174c781d797aa', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': "Trump’s CISA nominee denies Capitol was attacked on Jan. 6 Two senators subsequently said they would place holds on the nominee, who also refused to acknowledge Biden's 2020 electoral victory.", 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/threats/2026/11/trumps-cisa-nominee-denies-capitol-was-attacked-jan-6/417337/'}, {'signal_id': '9c17f68f8617b943', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Defense Business Brief: Vantor’s Raptor; Hadrian’s foundry, and more', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/business/2026/11/defense-business-brief-vantors-raptor-hadrians-foundry-and-more/417327/'}, {'signal_id': '36b61983904e0e60', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Appropriators slash Trump’s $17B Golden Dome request in draft bill GOP-led committee says reliance on reconciliation “threatens” the missile defense program’s success.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/policy/2026/11/appropriators-slash-trumps-17b-golden-dome-request-draft-bill/417326/'}, {'signal_id': 'a43bea9e6bec6793', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Need range time? The Army now has an online reservation system Officials say industry’s wait times for weapons testing has already plunged.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/defense-systems/2026/11/need-range-time-army-now-has-online-reservation-system/417309/'}, {'signal_id': '720a3bdce29026c0', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Major AI platforms generated viable plans for terrorist attacks, GAO finds Safety guardrails on ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and Grok failed to prevent federal investigators from developing detailed plans.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/threats/2026/11/major-ai-platforms-generated-viable-plans-terrorist-attacks-gao-finds/417308/'}, {'signal_id': 'f086773daea14700', 'source'